B.aHg=new A.S(B.KN,["Masari Premium","Premium","Navigation path: Premium hub, {current}","Premium hub","Home","Interest test","Test","Projects lab","Projects","Salary guide","Salaries","Practical guides","Guides","One space to understand your options and try them.","Profile","Premium Account","Back to Masari","Back to Premium","Choose how deep you want to go","A closer look before you decide","Sharper tests, richer articles, and projects that let you try a field instead of only reading about it.","Local development preview \u2014 nothing will be charged and no real payment will be made.","Purchases run only through the store provider, and entitlement is verified on the server.","Subscribing and payment are unavailable in this build because billing and verified products are not configured.","Open the projects lab \u2014 free for everyone","Open the Premium preview workspace","Open Premium","Activate local preview access","Premium access activated after verification.","The purchase could not be completed or verified.","Subscribe to Premium","Subscribing is unavailable in this build","Continue with the free version","Restore subscription","Your Premium subscription was restored.","Restoring a subscription is unavailable right now.","This is local preview access, not a subscription. It grants no production entitlement and is not a purchase.","Access is granted only after the server verifies a valid entitlement.","A payment provider, valid products and server verification are required before subscribing can be offered.","Free","Every exploration feature available today","A quick 15-question test","A basic exploratory result","Both the basic and the in-depth test","In-depth articles and tracks","Projects lab plus digital and financial guides","Best for exploring","A clear price before you subscribe","The price will appear here once a payment provider is connected. Nothing is charged in this preview.","What you walk away with","Premium turns exploring into a practical career decision you can test and develop.","A personal career direction based on your result","Salary comparison by country","Portfolio projects with saved progress","A deeper assessment and organised content","Pricing and payment will be switched on once the store subscription is connected.","Your career decision space","Do not stop at reading about a specialty.\nUnderstand it, try it, then decide.","A structured journey that starts with your interests, moves through practical content, and ends with a step you can take today.","Start by discovering your interests","Explore fields","Your library right now","fields","in-depth analyses","hands-on projects","{count} specialties","1 specialty","{count} branches","1 branch","{count} in-depth analyses","1 in-depth analysis","A clear route from curiosity to a decision","Discover","Start with your interests and strengths","Go deeper","Read what the field and specialty are really like","Try it","Build one small project","Decide","Turn what you learned into a step","Quick access","What do you want to do now?","Pick your goal directly; each tool leads to one clear step after it.","Explore by field","Every field in Masari","Start with a field, then filter its specialties and read the in-depth analyses tied to it.","Selected reading","Featured articles","Premium catalog v{version} \u2022 {count} articles completed in this batch. The rest of the specialties keep their free content until their articles are reviewed.","Structured analyses that take you from a general description to what a specialty is actually like.","Find your direction","The detailed interest test","A standalone 32-question test, saved automatically, with a fuller explanation.","Start the test","Learn by doing","Projects lab","45 tech projects for the Saudi market, with startup capital, a launch plan and an evaluation.","Pick a project","Future skills","The digital world","Security, artificial intelligence, freelancing and building products.","Browse the guides","Financial awareness","Trading basics","Learn about risk, analysis and fraud \u2014 with no trading recommendations.","Learn safely","Commerce today","E-commerce","Operating models, margin arithmetic, platforms, payments, logistics and the rules.","Understand commerce","Tomorrow\u2019s technology","Cryptocurrency and blockchain","A deep explanation of blockchain, each network\u2019s characteristics, practical use and career paths.","Understand blockchain","The economics of currencies","The foreign exchange market","Market structure, pricing, leverage, regulation, fraud and career paths.","Understand FX","Before any market","How to be a successful investor","Investing principles, valuation, risk management and a readiness checklist before any decision.","Start from the basics","Understand the market","Salary guide","Search documented salaries by specialty, country and sector.","Compare salaries","Career path plan","Complete the interest test first","A plan made for you","Practical steps based on your result \u2014 not a final verdict.","Assessment confidence","Assessment confidence: {label}{percentSuffix}","Assessment confidence: {label}{percentSuffix} \u2022 {count} recommendations","{match} \u2022 {skills} skills \u2022 {steps} next steps","Top suggested paths","The execution track, step by step","Each suggested path has its own checklist, split across five stages and built from that specialty\u2019s own content. Your progress is saved.","Open your personal career report","Update your plan after a deeper test, or after picking up new skills.","Why it may suit you","Skills to start with","Your next steps","Career path report","A summary you can save and share","Salary context","No salary figure is included until you choose a role and a country in the Premium salary guide.","Copy the report data","Report data copied","Copy the readable report","Readable report copied","This report is guidance, based on your assessment and Masari\u2019s reviewed content; it is not a final career or financial decision.","No specialties are available right now","Choose a specialty","Guide to documented salaries","Pick a specialty, then compare country, sector and experience wherever published data with a source and a review date is available.","Premium fields","Field not found","Search this field by name or branch","Clear search","Specialties","No matching results","Try another word, or clear the search.","The fields could not be loaded right now.","Explore this field","In depth","Read the in-depth analysis","View details","In-depth article","Article not found","In this article","Sources","Last reviewed","Editorially reviewed","Needs human clinical review","Needs expert review","Practical guides","Six domains, each one a full guide","Pick the field you want to understand. Each one is a series of guides ordered from the ground up, with a readiness checklist and a knowledge check.","Returns calculator","Pick a company, an amount and two years, and see what the amount actually became.","Company","Amount invested","From end of","To end of","The amount became","Gain","Loss","Total return","Annualised return","over {years} years","The same amount in the S&P 500","The stock beat the index over this period.","The stock trailed the index over this period.","What the amount was worth each year-end","The annualised figure is smoothed. The bars above show that no single year looked like it \u2014 and the gap between the two is exactly what is hard to sit through in practice.","Year-end closing prices adjusted for splits, with no dividends. For companies that pay them \u2014 Coca-Cola and Aramco here \u2014 the real return was higher than these figures show.","Data through {date}","This calculator explains what happened; it does not suggest buying anything. Picking a company we now know went up is not an investment decision \u2014 it is reading the result after it arrived.","An index, not a company","No prices for this company in the two years selected.","Price sources","Stocks","Stocks","One share means owning part of a company","What you are actually buying, how to read a global company, what separates a good business from a bad one, and valuation \u2014 with a calculator that shows what time did to a real amount.","Educational content, not financial advice and not a recommendation to buy or sell any particular share. The company names here are examples for explaining how a business is read, not investment suggestions. Past performance does not predict the future, and the shares of any company can lose most of their value \u2014 deal only with a licensed firm and a qualified professional.","Owning companies","Understand stocks","Trading basics","The digital world","Read the candle before you read the forecast","The anatomy of a candle, what its shapes mean, reversal and continuation patterns, risk management \u2014 and the limits of what any pattern can tell you.","Build your skills for the digital world","Practical guides to security, artificial intelligence, freelancing and building products.","Educational content, not financial advice. Candlestick patterns describe what happened, they do not predict what will: no pattern beats chance by a margin you can lean on by itself. Leveraged trading can cost you your entire capital, and figures published by regulators show most retail accounts lose money. Masari contains no buy or sell recommendations.","Try the linked project","Tap to enlarge","Close image","Trading","Digital","E-commerce","Commerce","Understand e-commerce as an operation, not a storefront","From operating models and margin arithmetic to platforms, payments, logistics, marketing, the Saudi regulatory picture and career paths.","Educational material for understanding how e-commerce works. It is not investment, legal or tax advice, and not a promise of profit. Most new stores do not turn a profit in their first year \u2014 check the official authority in your country before any financial commitment.","Cryptocurrencies","Crypto","Understand blockchain from the ground up","From block structure and consensus mechanisms to each network\u2019s characteristics, practical use and career paths.","Educational content about the technology. It is not financial advice and not an invitation to buy or sell any digital asset. Digital assets are highly volatile and can lose all their value, and regulations differ between countries \u2014 check the official authority in your country.","The foreign exchange market","FX","Understand the FX market as an economic machine","From market structure, pricing and currency drivers to the arithmetic of leverage, the regulatory picture, fraud patterns and career paths.","Educational content about the FX market. It is not financial advice and not a recommendation to trade or to use any broker. Leveraged currency trading can lose your entire capital, and regulators\u2019 data show most retail accounts lose money \u2014 verify any firm\u2019s licence with the official authority in your country.","How to be a successful investor in any market","Investing","Principles that apply to every market","What investing is, time horizon and compounding, where value comes from, cycles and FOMO, valuation, risk management and the written plan.","Educational content about investing principles. It is not financial advice and not a recommendation to buy or sell any asset. Nobody guarantees a return, the market bottom cannot be known in advance, and every investment can lose capital \u2014 deal only with a licensed entity and consult a qualified professional.","Readiness checklist","{done} of {total}","{done} of {total} steps completed","{total} knowledge steps that measure what you actually understand before any decision.","You have completed {done} of {total} steps.","Back to the {category} guides","Reset the checklist","Completing the list measures your understanding only. This content is educational, not financial advice; nobody guarantees a return, and every dealing in financial markets can lose your entire capital.","Knowledge check","This section has no check yet.","Test your understanding after reading the guides: {total} questions with an explanation for every answer.","Best score {percent}% across {attempts} attempts.","{total} questions","Good understanding is {percent}% or above, and retakes are unlimited.","Best {best}% \u2022 last {last}% \u2022 {attempts} attempts.","Start the check","Retake the check","Model {number} of {total}","The check has {total} different models. Each time you open it you get the next one, and after the last it returns to the first.","Retake with a new model","Next up: model {number} of {total}","Open the check","A bank of {total} questions across {models} models","Your score","A B C D E","{answered} of {total}","Question {index} of {total}","Correct","Not correct","Next question","Finish and see the result","You answered {correct} of {total} correctly","You passed the {percent}% mark.","Not at {percent}% yet. Re-read the guides and take it again \u2014 retakes are always available.","Your best score is {best}% across {attempts} attempts.","Review the questions","Correct answer: {answer}","Read the related guide","Back to the guides","Account settings","Guest, no account","Premium membership active","Membership inactive","Status","Source","Expires","No expiry date","Readiness checklists","Back to the tools and guides dashboard.","Export my data","A JSON copy of your preferences and results.","Back to the free version","Your membership stays as it is, and you can return to Premium at any time.","Account page in the free version","{percent}% match","{percent}%",", ","Execution track: {specialty}","Steps built from this specialty\u2019s own content, split across {count} stages. Pick the stage you are at.","{count} years","The in-depth paths currently cover architecture, medicine, business administration and information technology, and keep expanding to the rest.","Try a field before you commit to it","Pick a small project, work through its steps, and keep an output you can add to your portfolio. No project guarantees income or a job.","Progress could not be saved. Try again.","Project finished \u2014 great work!","Completed","Problem","Outcome","Tools","Skills","Steps to build it","Portfolio output","Commercial potential","Warning","You finished this stage. Move on to the next one.","Explore","Go deeper","Reality check","Prepare to apply","Apply and follow up","Understand what the field is like before you invest time in it.","Look at what you would actually study, not at the title.","Test your assumptions in the real world before you commit.","Get the admission requirements ready before the application season.","Submit your application and follow it through to the result."],t.w)
